  {
   "_id": 9840,
   "ANSWER": "<h3 data-end=\"154\" data-start=\"94\"><strong data-end=\"152\" data-start=\"98\">1. Role of TCP in Reliable Communication (4 marks)</strong></h3>\n\n<ul data-end=\"364\" data-start=\"155\">\n\t<li data-end=\"201\" data-start=\"155\">\n\t<p data-end=\"201\" data-start=\"157\">TCP is a <strong data-end=\"198\" data-start=\"166\">connection-oriented protocol</strong>.</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"267\" data-start=\"202\">\n\t<p data-end=\"267\" data-start=\"204\">Ensures <strong data-end=\"229\" data-start=\"212\">data delivery</strong>, <strong data-end=\"240\" data-start=\"231\">order</strong>, and <strong data-end=\"264\" data-start=\"246\">error checking</strong>.</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"364\" data-start=\"268\">\n\t<p data-end=\"364\" data-start=\"270\">Suitable for applications where <strong data-end=\"329\" data-start=\"302\">reliability is critical</strong> (e.g., messaging, file transfers).</p>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n\n<hr data-end=\"369\" data-start=\"366\" />\n<h3 data-end=\"427\" data-start=\"371\"><strong data-end=\"425\" data-start=\"375\">2. Python TCP Server and Client Code (7 marks)</strong></h3>\n\n<p data-end=\"440\" data-start=\"429\"><strong data-end=\"440\" data-start=\"429\">Server:</strong></p>\n\n<p data-end=\"440\" data-start=\"429\"><strong data-end=\"440\" data-start=\"429\">import socket</strong></p>\n\n<p><strong data-end=\"440\" data-start=\"429\">server = socket.socket()<br />\nserver.bind((&#39;localhost&#39;, 12345))<br />\nserver.listen(1)<br />\nconn, addr = server.accept()<br />\nprint(&quot;Connected:&quot;, addr)<br />\ndata = conn.recv(1024)<br />\nprint(&quot;Received:&quot;, data.decode())<br />\nconn.close()</strong></p>\n\n<p><strong data-end=\"440\" data-start=\"429\">Client:</strong></p>\n\n<p>import socket</p>\n\n<p>client = socket.socket()<br />\nclient.connect((&#39;localhost&#39;, 12345))<br />\nclient.send(b&quot;Hello Server&quot;)<br />\nclient.close()</p>\n\n<h3 data-end=\"885\" data-start=\"825\"><strong data-end=\"883\" data-start=\"829\">3. Real-World Communication + Limitation (4 marks)</strong></h3>\n\n<ul data-end=\"1044\" data-start=\"886\">\n\t<li data-end=\"966\" data-start=\"886\">\n\t<p data-end=\"966\" data-start=\"888\">Models a <strong data-end=\"912\" data-start=\"897\">chat system</strong>: server listens, client connects and sends message.</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"1044\" data-start=\"967\">\n\t<p data-end=\"1044\" data-start=\"969\"><strong data-end=\"983\" data-start=\"969\">Limitation</strong>: Doesn&#39;t support multiple clients or asynchronous messaging.</p>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n",
   "COURSE_CODE": "21CSC203P",
   "LEVEL": 3,
   "OUTCOMES": [
    "PLO4",
    "PLO2",
    "PLO1"
   ],
   "QUESTION_DESC": "<p data-end=\"394\" data-start=\"150\">You are developing a Python-based chat application where messages must be reliably delivered between users. The system should allow one server and multiple clients to exchange messages over a stable connection using TCP sockets.</p>\n\n<p data-end=\"405\" data-start=\"396\"><strong data-end=\"405\" data-start=\"396\">Task:</strong></p>\n\n<ol data-end=\"777\" data-start=\"407\">\n\t<li data-end=\"495\" data-start=\"407\">\n\t<p data-end=\"495\" data-start=\"410\"><strong data-end=\"421\" data-start=\"410\">Explain</strong> the role of TCP in ensuring reliable network communication. <em data-end=\"493\" data-start=\"482\">(4 marks)</em></p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"651\" data-start=\"496\">\n\t<p data-end=\"651\" data-start=\"499\"><strong data-end=\"520\" data-start=\"499\">Write Python code</strong> to create a basic TCP server that accepts client connections and a client script that sends a message to the server. <em data-end=\"649\" data-start=\"638\">(7 marks)</em></p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"777\" data-start=\"652\">\n\t<p data-end=\"777\" data-start=\"655\"><strong data-end=\"667\" data-start=\"655\">Describe</strong> how this implementation models real-world client-server communication and mention one limitation. <em data-end=\"777\" data-start=\"766\">(4 marks)</em></p>\n\t</li>\n</ol>\n\n<p data-end=\"492\" data-start=\"153\">&nbsp;</p>\n",
